  <div class="fcx" aria-label="HVLS Fans Manufacturers in Ahmedabad">
<section class="fcx-band"><div class="fcx-wrap"><div class="fcx-duo"><div class="fcx-panel"><span class="fcx-ico"><i class="fas fa-circle-question"></i></span><h2>What Are HVLS Fans?</h2><p>HVLS stands for High Volume Low Speed. These fans have large-diameter blades that rotate at very low speeds while moving a large volume of air. Their design makes them appropriate for buildings where traditional smaller fans may not provide uniform air movement across the entire floor area.</p><p>HVLS fans are especially useful in large open areas where maintaining continuous air circulation is essential. The airflow produced by the large blades can help reduce stagnant air and create a more comfortable environment for employees, visitors, and occupants.</p></div><div class="fcx-panel"><span class="fcx-ico"><i class="fas fa-rotate"></i></span><h2>How HVLS Fans Work</h2><p>HVLS fans use large aerofoil-shaped blades to move air downward and outward across a wide area. As the air reaches the floor, it spreads horizontally and gradually circulates through the surrounding space.</p><p>The large diameter of the fan allows one unit to cover a much larger area than a traditional small fan. According to the Ahmedabad product range, these fans can circulate air across about 20 metres from the fan's centre in all directions.</p><p>This makes HVLS fans appropriate for warehouses, manufacturing facilities, logistics centres, and other buildings with large floor areas and high ceilings.</p></div></div></div></section><section class="fcx-band fcx-band--alt"><div class="fcx-wrap"><h2>Key Features of HVLS Fans</h2><p>HVLS fans are designed with features that support large-area air movement and energy-efficient operation.</p><ul class="fcx-checks"><li>High Volume Low Speed technology</li><li>Large aerofoil blades</li><li>Available in 12 ft to 24 ft range</li><li>Airflow coverage from 229,000 CFM to 377,000 CFM</li><li>Air circulation across approximately 20 metres from the fan centre</li><li>Designed for large indoor areas</li><li>Suitable for warehouses and factory sheds</li><li>Useful for logistics hubs and large halls</li><li>Supports comfortable and consistent air movement</li><li>Designed to provide maximum airflow with controlled power consumption</li></ul><p>The aerofoil blade design helps generate effective airflow while supporting efficient fan operation.</p></div></section><section class="fcx-band"><div class="fcx-wrap"><h2>Technical Specifications</h2><div class="fcx-spec"><table class="fcx-table"><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Product</th><td>HVLS Fans</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Full Form</th><td>High Volume Low Speed</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Fan Range</th><td>12 ft to 24 ft</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Airflow Coverage</th><td>229,000 CFM to 377,000 CFM</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Air Circulation</th><td>Approximately 20 metres from fan centre</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Blade Design</th><td>Aerofoil Blades</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Operating Principle</th><td>High Volume, Low Speed</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Main Purpose</th><td>Large-Area Air Circulation</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Typical Spaces</th><td>Warehouses, Factory Sheds, Logistics Hubs, Gyms &amp; Large Halls</td></tr></tbody></table><div class="fcx-note"><span class="fcx-ico"><i class="fas fa-sliders"></i></span><div><p>These specifications are based on the current Ahmedabad HVLS fan range listed by FanAir. Final selection should consider the required airflow, static pressure, building design, and site conditions.</p></div></div></div></div></section><section class="fcx-band fcx-band--alt"><div class="fcx-wrap"><div class="fcx-center"><h2>Applications of HVLS Fans</h2></div><p class="fcx-lead">HVLS fans may be used in many large commercial, industrial, and institutional spaces in which traditional air movement may not be sufficient.</p><div class="fcx-cards fcx-cards--3"><div class="fcx-card"><span class="fcx-ico"><i class="fas fa-warehouse"></i></span><h3>Warehouses</h3><p>Large warehouses often have high ceilings and large floor areas. HVLS fans can help circulate air across these areas and reduce stagnant air zones.</p></div><div class="fcx-card"><span class="fcx-ico"><i class="fas fa-industry"></i></span><h3>Factory Sheds</h3><p>Manufacturing facilities and factory sheds can become uncomfortable when air movement is limited. Large-diameter fans can provide continuous circulation across production and working areas.</p></div><div class="fcx-card"><span class="fcx-ico"><i class="fas fa-warehouse"></i></span><h3>Logistics Hubs</h3><p>Distribution centres and logistics facilities commonly have large open floor areas with frequent movement of people and materials. HVLS fans can support better air movement across these areas.</p></div><div class="fcx-card"><span class="fcx-ico"><i class="fas fa-people-group"></i></span><h3>Gyms</h3><p>Gyms and fitness facilities require good air movement due to continuous occupant activity. HVLS fans can offer broad airflow without requiring a large number of small fans.</p></div><div class="fcx-card"><span class="fcx-ico"><i class="fas fa-people-group"></i></span><h3>Large Halls</h3><p>Auditoriums, halls, and other spacious indoor areas can use HVLS systems where large-area air movement is needed.</p><p>The Ahmedabad product page specifically lists warehouses, factory sheds, logistics hubs, gyms, and large halls among the applications for these fans.</p></div></div></div></section><section class="fcx-band"><div class="fcx-wrap"><h2>Benefits of HVLS Fans</h2><p>Installing a properly selected HVLS fan can provide various practical benefits:</p><ul class="fcx-checks"><li>Wide airflow coverage across large floor areas</li><li>Helps improve overall air movement</li><li>Suitable for high-ceiling buildings</li><li>Can reduce stagnant air in large spaces</li><li>Requires fewer large fans compared with multiple small circulation fans in some layouts</li><li>Aerofoil blades support efficient airflow</li><li>Suitable for continuous air movement</li><li>Useful across commercial and industrial environments</li><li>Can contribute to a more comfortable indoor operating environment</li></ul><p>The actual performance depends on factors such as building dimensions, ceiling height, fan placement, airflow requirements, and operating conditions.</p></div></section><section class="fcx-band fcx-band--alt"><div class="fcx-wrap"><div class="fcx-blocks"><div class="fcx-block"><h2>HVLS Fans Suppliers in Ahmedabad</h2><p>Ahmedabad and the wider Gujarat industrial area have many large facilities where effective air movement is essential. Industrial areas around Vatva, Naroda, Changodar, and Sanand include textile mills, chemical and pharmaceutical plants, engineering units, and automotive facilities.</p><p>For these environments, HVLS fans can provide a practical solution for circulating air across large floor areas. The fan size and configuration should be selected according to the space, airflow requirement, and site conditions.</p></div><div class="fcx-block"><h2>HVLS Fans Manufacturer in India</h2><p>The HVLS fans supplied for Ahmedabad projects are manufactured at the FanAir facility in Neemrana, Rajasthan. Each unit is selected according to the specified airflow, static pressure, and site conditions of the project.</p><p>Technical data and sizing support may be provided before ordering. Finished equipment can then be dispatched to Ahmedabad and other places across India.</p></div></div></div></section><section class="fcx-band"><div class="fcx-wrap"><h2>How to Choose the Right HVLS Fan</h2><p>Selecting the proper HVLS fan requires consideration of the entire building and ventilation requirements.</p><ul class="fcx-checks fcx-checks--long"><li><b>Area size:</b> Check the total floor area that needs air movement.</li><li><b>Ceiling height:</b> Consider the height of the building before selecting the fan size.</li><li><b>Required airflow:</b> Determine the required CFM according to the application.</li><li><b>Fan diameter:</b> Select a suitable diameter from the available range.</li><li><b>Fan placement:</b> Plan fan locations to achieve effective and uniform air movement.</li><li><b>Building use:</b> Warehouses, factories, gyms, and logistics facilities may have different requirements.</li><li><b>Site conditions:</b> Consider structural and installation conditions before final selection.</li></ul><p>Sharing the building dimensions, ceiling height, application, and required airflow can help in selecting a suitable HVLS fan configuration.</p></div></section><section class="fcx-band fcx-band--alt"><div class="fcx-wrap"><div class="fcx-center"><h2>FAQs</h2></div><div class="fcx-faq"><details><summary>What does HVLS stand for?</summary><p>HVLS stands for High Volume Low Speed. These fans move large quantities of air at low speeds and are designed for large indoor areas.</p></details><details><summary>What sizes of HVLS fans are available?</summary><p>The Ahmedabad range includes HVLS fans from 12 ft to 24 ft.</p></details><details><summary>What airflow can HVLS fans offer?</summary><p>The listed HVLS fans provide airflow coverage ranging from 229,000 CFM to 377,000 CFM, depending on the selected configuration.</p></details><details><summary>Where are HVLS fans usually used?</summary><p>HVLS fans are generally used in warehouses, factory sheds, logistics hubs, gyms, and large halls where wide-area air movement is required.</p></details><details><summary>How much area can an HVLS fan circulate air throughout?</summary><p>The Ahmedabad product information states that the fans can circulate air across about 20 metres from the fan's centre in all directions. Actual coverage can vary according to building and installation conditions.</p></details></div><div class="fcx-center" style="margin-top:26px"><a href="product.php" class="btn-cyber btn-cyber--primary fcx-btn" title="Fan Air India Products">Learn More <i class="fas fa-arrow-right"></i></a></div></div></section><section class="fcx-band"><div class="fcx-wrap"><div class="fcx-cta"><h2>Conclusion</h2><p>HVLS fans provide an effective approach to air movement in large indoor areas. Their large aerofoil blades, high-volume airflow, and low-speed operation make them suitable for warehouses, factory sheds, logistics hubs, gyms, and large halls.</p><p>FanAir India Pvt. Ltd. manufactures HVLS fans at its Neemrana facility and supplies them to Ahmedabad and other locations throughout India. Proper selection based on floor area, ceiling height, airflow requirements, and site conditions can help achieve effective and consistent ventilation.</p><a href="../contact.php" class="fcx-cta__btn" title="Contact Fan Air India">Contact Us <i class="fas fa-arrow-right"></i></a></div></div></section>
  </div>



